  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Topics, Partitions & the Log",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Topic Is Not A Queue",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Topic = named logical stream of records, a category.",
            "Not a queue with one tail; it has no single tail.",
            "Partition = real unit of storage and parallelism.",
            "A topic is just a set of N partitions."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Each partition is an append-only, immutable, ordered commit log. Writes only ever land at the end."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Offsets Live In A Partition"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Offset = monotonically increasing 64-bit integer.",
            "Assigned by the partition leader on append.",
            "Unique WITHIN a partition, never across the topic.",
            "Partition 0 and partition 1 both hold an offset 42."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Record field",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "key",
              "nullable, picks partition"
            ],
            [
              "value",
              "nullable, null = tombstone"
            ],
            [
              "timestamp",
              "create or log-append"
            ],
            [
              "headers",
              "metadata, not keyed"
            ],
            [
              "partition, offset",
              "assigned, not sent"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reads Are Non-Destructive"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Consuming does not delete the record.",
            "N consumer groups read the same bytes independently.",
            "Position = one stored integer per group/topic/partition.",
            "Stored in the `__consumer_offsets` topic."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Partition On Disk"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "ls /kafka-logs/orders-3/   # topic orders, part 3",
            "00000000000000012345.log   # named by base offset",
            "00000000000000012345.index    # offset -> byte pos",
            "00000000000000012345.timeindex  # ts -> offset"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Segments",
          "items": [
            "Default roll at 1 GB or 7 days.",
            "Only the newest (active) segment is written.",
            "Older segments immutable, eligible for cleanup.",
            "Indexes let a broker seek without scanning."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Retention Deletes Segments"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`retention.ms` and `retention.bytes` drive deletion.",
            "Whole segments are dropped, never single records.",
            "So you cannot delete one bad record by retention."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "40",
              "41",
              "42 HW",
              "43",
              "44 LEO"
            ],
            "caption": "partition log"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Topics, Partitions & the Log (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "LEO vs HW",
          "text": "LEO = next offset to be written. HW = highest offset replicated to all ISR. Consumers read only up to the HW, so a lost leader can never un-deliver data."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Promise",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Total order WITHIN a partition. Nothing more.",
            "No global ordering across partitions. Ever, at any config.",
            "Different partitions = no defined relative order.",
            "True even if the two writes are microseconds apart."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Corollary: order is preserved only for records that share a partition, which in practice means records that share a key."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Still Holds"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One consumer on one partition sees exact append order.",
            "Ordering survives replication: followers copy in order.",
            "Plain producer: per-partition, per-producer-session only.",
            "Retries can reorder without idempotence (see ch. 6)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "RabbitMQ",
                "lines": [
                  "Per-queue FIFO",
                  "Global order per queue",
                  "Scale = more queues",
                  "Order vs fanout"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Kafka",
                "lines": [
                  "Per-partition FIFO",
                  "No topic-wide order",
                  "Scale = more partitions",
                  "Order traded for scale"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Design Rule: Pick The Key"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "// ledger: order per account, not globally",
            "var r = new ProducerRecord<>(",
            "  \"ledger\", txn.accountId(), txn.toJson());",
            "// same accountId -> same partition -> ordered"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Order Quietly Dies"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Adding partitions re-maps keys; old and new split apart.",
            "Multi-topic ordering is undefined: `payments` vs `orders`.",
            "Consumer thread pool per record destroys it app-side.",
            "Fix: a key-hash executor, one worker per key bucket."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Timestamps Do Not Save You",
          "items": [
            "Log-append time: monotonic per partition only.",
            "Create time: client-supplied, can go backwards.",
            "Sorting by timestamp is not a total order."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ordering vs Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Partition",
            "Lag",
            "Reader sees"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "p2",
              "0.4 s",
              "near-live"
            ],
            [
              "p5",
              "6 min",
              "6 min behind"
            ],
            [
              "p9",
              "0.9 s",
              "near-live"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Ordering is not delivery timing. Lag differs per partition, so p5 can trail p2 by minutes with both perfectly ordered."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Ordering Guarantees",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "One Line",
          "text": "Kafka orders a key, not a topic. If two events must be sequenced, make them share a key."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Client Decides",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The producer, not the broker, picks the partition.",
            "Assignment happens client-side before the network call.",
            "With a key: `murmur2(keyBytes) % numPartitions`.",
            "Kafka's own murmur2, not Java `hashCode()`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Same key plus same partition count gives the same partition forever, across producers, client languages and restarts."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "key bytes",
              "murmur2",
              "% numPartitions",
              "partition 7",
              "batch",
              "broker"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Null Key Behaviour"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Client",
            "Rule",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "2.4+",
              "sticky partitioner",
              "fill one batch, switch"
            ],
            [
              "<2.4",
              "round-robin per record",
              "many tiny batches"
            ],
            [
              "any",
              "explicit partition",
              "overrides everything"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "new ProducerRecord<>(\"orders\",",
            "    order.customerId(),  // key = 2nd arg",
            "    payload);            // not a header!"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Custom Partitioner"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "// implement Partitioner, then:",
            "props.put(\"partitioner.class\", \"com.io.GeoP\");",
            "// partition(topic,key,keyBytes,value,",
            "//   valueBytes,cluster) -> int"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use for tenant isolation or geo-affinity.",
            "Or to pin a hot key to a dedicated partition.",
            "Explicit partition is the escape hatch and the skew maker."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cardinality & Hot Keys"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Key cardinality must far exceed partition count.",
            "3 keys over 12 partitions uses 3, leaves 9 empty.",
            "Hot key = one key with a huge share of traffic.",
            "It pins to one partition; that partition is the bottleneck."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hot Key Fixes",
          "items": [
            "Composite key: `userId#bucket`.",
            "Key salting across a small suffix range.",
            "Two-stage aggregate, shard then combine.",
            "Each one costs strict per-user order."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Keys & Partitioners",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keys Drive Compaction"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compaction retains the latest value per key.",
            "A null key makes a record uncompactable.",
            "Tombstone = key present, VALUE null = delete this key."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Gotcha",
          "text": "The key serializer must be stable. Switching a key from String to Avro encoding changes the bytes, so murmur2 re-partitions every key silently."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Parallelism Ceiling",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "At most one consumer per partition within a group.",
            "20 partitions + 30 consumers = 10 idle, permanently.",
            "Extra consumers past that buy zero throughput.",
            "Add partitions, or split the work downstream."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Multiple groups scale independently. Each group gets its own full assignment of all partitions."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "topic: orders (12 parts)",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1",
                "b2"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0"
              ],
              [
                "c2_0"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "topic: orders (12 parts)",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "group billing"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "group search"
              },
              "b2": {
                "text": "group audit"
              },
              "c0_0": {
                "text": "6 consumers, 2 each"
              },
              "c1_0": {
                "text": "12 consumers, 1 each"
              },
              "c2_0": {
                "text": "1 consumer, all 12"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b0"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b1"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b2"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_0"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rough Sizing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "parts = max(target / producer_rate,",
            "            target / consumer_rate)",
            "# per-partition write often 10 MB/s+",
            "# consumer processing cost binds first"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One-Way Door"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Partitions can only be INCREASED, never decreased.",
            "`kafka-topics.sh --alter --partitions 24` is one-way.",
            "Increasing re-maps the hash space; keys move.",
            "Per-key order and compaction history both break."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Never In Place",
          "text": "Do not increase partitions on a compacted topic. The same key can then exist in two partitions and the table view is corrupt."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Partitions Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Where",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Broker",
              "open file handles"
            ],
            [
              "Broker",
              "index buffer memory"
            ],
            [
              "Follower",
              "one fetch stream each"
            ],
            [
              "Cluster",
              "leader election time"
            ],
            [
              "Producer",
              "`batch.size` per partition"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Partition Count & Regret",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "1000 partitions x 32 KB = 32 MB of buffer pressure.",
            "Metadata propagation scales with total partition count.",
            "That is a controller failover concern, not a topic one.",
            "KRaft removes the ZooKeeper metadata bottleneck.",
            "Per-broker file and memory cost stays regardless."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Trade-off Row"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Few partitions",
            "Many partitions"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tighter ordering",
              "high parallelism"
            ],
            [
              "cheap metadata",
              "slower failover"
            ],
            [
              "weak parallelism",
              "longer rebalances"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rule Of Thumb",
          "text": "Start with a count you can live with for a year. Modest over-provisioning beats resharding a live keyed topic."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RF = number of copies of each partition.",
            "Copies are placed on distinct brokers.",
            "Each partition has one leader and RF-1 followers.",
            "Assignment is per-partition, not per-topic."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "All produces and, by default, all consumes go through the leader. Followers are pure replicas with no client traffic."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Followers Catch Up"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Followers issue normal fetch requests to the leader.",
            "Same protocol a consumer uses. No special channel.",
            "Leadership is spread so no broker carries them all.",
            "3 brokers, 6 partitions = 2 leaderships each."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "RF",
            "Use",
            "Loss of 1 broker"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "scratch / dev",
              "data gone forever"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "rare",
              "no write headroom"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "production default",
              "still writable"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Fault Tolerance",
          "text": "RF-1 broker failures are survivable for availability. Durability limits are tighter and are set by acks and ISR, not by RF alone."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Changing RF Later"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# set once at creation:",
            "kafka-topics.sh --create --replication-factor 3",
            "# change later only with a JSON plan:",
            "kafka-reassign-partitions.sh --throttle 50000000"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reassignment copies whole partitions over the network.",
            "Throttle it or it starves live traffic.",
            "`broker.rack` spreads replicas across racks and AZs.",
            "One AZ loss then cannot take every copy."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Preferred Leader"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Preferred leader = first replica in the assignment list.",
            "`auto.leader.rebalance.enable` restores it after recovery.",
            "Without it, leaderships pile onto surviving brokers."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Replication, Leaders & Followers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Storage Math",
          "items": [
            "RF multiplies disk, always.",
            "1 TB of topic data at RF=3 = 3 TB cluster disk.",
            "Plus retention headroom on top."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Escape Hatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "KIP-392 fetch",
                "lines": [
                  "Read nearby replica",
                  "Cuts cross-AZ cost",
                  "Slight staleness",
                  "Safe trade"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Unclean election",
                "lines": [
                  "Stale replica leads",
                  "Availability bought",
                  "Silent data loss",
                  "Document it"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Watch",
          "text": "`unclean.leader.election.enable=true` lets an out-of-sync replica take over. Committed records disappear without an error anywhere."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What ISR Means",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ISR = replicas, leader included, caught up with the leader.",
            "Caught up = fetched within `replica.lag.time.max.ms`.",
            "Default 30s. Time-based, not message-count-based.",
            "Lagging follower is removed; rejoins at the leader's LEO."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Why Not Message Count",
          "text": "Old `replica.lag.max.messages` was removed: a legitimate traffic burst falsely evicted perfectly healthy followers."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "High Watermark"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "HW = min LEO across the current ISR.",
            "Records at or below the HW are committed.",
            "Only committed records are visible to consumers."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "L:108",
              "F1:108",
              "F2:105",
              "HW=105"
            ],
            "caption": "ISR LEOs"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The acks Table"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "acks",
            "Waits for",
            "Loses on"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0",
              "nothing",
              "any failure"
            ],
            [
              "1",
              "leader log write",
              "leader dies first"
            ],
            [
              "all / -1",
              "every ISR member",
              "ISR shrunk to 1"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`acks=0` is fire and forget: highest throughput, zero durability. `acks=all` is the same flag as `acks=-1`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "acks=all Is Not Enough"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "If ISR shrinks to just the leader, \"all\" means one replica.",
            "`min.insync.replicas` is the guard, set per broker or topic.",
            "ISR size below it: acks=all produces fail.",
            "Error is `NotEnoughReplicasException`, not silent loss."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ISR & The Durability Contract",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "replication.factor=3",
            "min.insync.replicas=2   # refuse below 2 copies",
            "acks=all                # producer side",
            "enable.idempotence=true # default in 3.0+"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking min.insync"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "RF / min.isr",
            "One broker down"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "3 / 1",
              "writes ok, durability theatre"
            ],
            [
              "3 / 2",
              "writes ok, 2 copies held"
            ],
            [
              "3 / 3",
              "topic stops accepting writes"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Always True",
          "text": "Raising min.insync.replicas increases durability and decreases write availability. There is no setting where it does both."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Idempotent Producer"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Adds a producer id plus a per-partition sequence number.",
            "Retries then cannot duplicate or reorder a record.",
            "Requires `max.in.flight.requests.per.connection` <= 5.",
            "Without it, in-flight > 1 plus retries can reorder."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Group Anatomy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Group = consumers sharing a `group.id`.",
            "The group owns every partition exactly once.",
            "Group coordinator: a broker, tracks membership.",
            "Group leader: a consumer, computes the assignment."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "member joins",
              "coordinator",
              "leader computes",
              "assignment",
              "fetch"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rebalance Triggers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A member joins the group.",
            "A member leaves cleanly.",
            "A member times out.",
            "Topic metadata changes, e.g. new partitions."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Assignors"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Assignor",
